-- Makes the reason of an entry in the admin optional (#1186): `match_edits.reason` may be empty. Editors typed the same word again and again ("Wikipedia", "Transfermarkt"), and the log has no use for it, so this also clears every reason that a person wrote and that contains one of those two words, in any case: in `match_edits.reason`, in `audit_log.reason` and, for `person.edit`, in the part ". Reden: …" at the end of `audit_log.detail`. A reason of the importer (an entry of `audit_log` without an account) stays.
-- The statements can run again: MariaDB cannot undo DDL, so a migration that stopped halfway finishes on the next start. After the first run no reason with those words is left.
-- It cannot be undone: the reasons that are cleared are gone. A backup from before the migration has them. To make the column required again, first give every empty reason a text.
ALTER TABLE `match_edits` MODIFY COLUMN `reason` varchar(300);--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `match_edits` SET `reason` = NULL WHERE LOWER(`reason`) LIKE '%wikipedia%' OR LOWER(`reason`) LIKE '%transfermarkt%';--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `audit_log` SET `reason` = NULL WHERE `user_id` IS NOT NULL AND (LOWER(`reason`) LIKE '%wikipedia%' OR LOWER(`reason`) LIKE '%transfermarkt%');--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `audit_log` SET `detail` = LEFT(`detail`, LOCATE('. Reden: ', `detail`)) WHERE `action` = 'person.edit' AND LOCATE('. Reden: ', `detail`) > 0 AND (LOWER(SUBSTRING(`detail`, LOCATE('. Reden: ', `detail`))) LIKE '%wikipedia%' OR LOWER(SUBSTRING(`detail`, LOCATE('. Reden: ', `detail`))) LIKE '%transfermarkt%');
